{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463238-lupus-gnosis-issue","id":1463238,"title":"Lupus Gnosis Issue?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-09T10:32:17-07:00","id":1463238,"title":"Lupus Gnosis Issue?","content":"I'm an old hat in online games, enough an old hat that I've seen a lot of limiting of the lupus breed in play. While some say lupus are just impossible to play (not true), others say lupus should be limited hardly for their gnosis 5.<br /> <br /> This gnosis 5 is used as a huge stopgap. Enough that I've seen people demand more limits to the breed in addition to the character creation ability restrictions.<br /> <br /> One thing I have almost never seen done is lowering the gnosis score. I myself would prefer lupus to have 3 like the metis, rather than 5.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T11:36:26-07:00","id":1463244,"title":"","content":"Well, in our LARP we have no lupus, because not spending time in breed form is a renown reduction, but since all players are humans in real life, we play homid or occasional metis. A human pretending to be a wolf might work well in Cosplay-circles, but we deem it silly in a way too distracting form the topics we usually incorporate in out game.<br /> <br /> I agree, that it isn't impossible to play lupus. It is, imo, nigh impossible to get people to agree on how a lupus should be played. We all are human and entertain that homids have a huge bandwidth of characteristics, even within the constraining archetypes of tribe and auspice. In my experience, it is, harder for players to be okay if someone else at the table plays a lupus different to what they believe a lupus should be played and that is even more true in games with a lot of players like LARPs or Online games.<br /> <br /> That said, we have an alternate character creation system, where breed doesn't dictate a starting gnosis, but dictate a bandwidth of suitable Gnosis starting values, depending on rank. Since all dot need to be bought with character creation experience points, choosing a lupus isn't getting you 20XP worth of Gnosis points simply because you choose lupus (compared to homid). So, yes, you could create a lupus with Gnosis 3 in our game. Also, envy about this costly feature is removed, by the alternate character creation approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T14:38:25-07:00","id":1463255,"title":"","content":"Having a lot of experience with the online larger game communities... I've found that the anti-lupus sentiment is finally starting to go away simply because the remaining diehards that want 50+ people in a single chat based game have started to rebel against the overly restrictive attitudes of the 00s.<br /> <br /> The biggest problem with the lupus, as someone that's run WtA in such a thing, is really how certain concepts need lots of Gnosis, and lupus are an easy pick for lots of Gnosis, so lupus concepts get very narrow because a lot of people are just trying to make an effective character.<br /> <br /> To that end, while I don't think it helps in large chats because those tend to be house rule avers, I did this years ago:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/37193-house-rule-balanced-starting-advantages\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/37193-house-rule-balanced-starting-advantages\"> House Rule: Balanced Starting Advantages - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/37193-house-rule-balanced-starting-advantages\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/37193-house-rule-balanced-starting-advantages </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I was asked to repost something I did on the old forums so here we go. The problem being addressed with the incredibly uneven levels of points you get by splat. A Ragabash Homid Glasswalker gets Rage 1/Gnosis 1/Willpower 3. An Ahroun Lupus Child of Gaia gets Rage 5, Gnosis 5, Willpower 4. For the </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I've gotten a lot of positive feedback from smaller online chat games (10-20 players) for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T04:28:17-07:00","id":1463572,"title":"","content":"I have been sincerely feeling that gnosis 1 is way too low for any type of play - even more so for theurge-types. And the experience/bp gap from gnosis 1 (homid) to 5 (lupus) is just too ridiculous. <br /> <br /> I am thinking that it'd be better to level gnosis at some level (say, 3) for all breeds and making the inconveniences from breeds (metis or lupus) give extra xp during play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T05:38:42-07:00","id":1463579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463238-lupus-gnosis-issue?p=1463572#post1463572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been sincerely feeling that gnosis 1 is way too low for any type of play - even more so for theurge-types. And the experience/bp gap from gnosis 1 (homid) to 5 (lupus) is just too ridiculous.<br /> <br /> I am thinking that it'd be better to level gnosis at some level (say, 3) for all breeds and making the inconveniences from breeds (metis or lupus) give extra xp during play.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally like 2/3/4 for the breeds.<br /> <br /> I don't think the non-homid breeds -need- extra XP, they have unique gifts and things they can call upon that homids cannot.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T10:22:47-07:00","id":1463598,"title":"","content":"I think lupus falls into the same category as other challenging rp concepts, like Red Talons or reformed BSD or whatever. It can be done, but only by mature, thoughtful players who have enough experience to play such concepts responsibly. Thus I'd say the problem isn't with the numbers or concept, but the motivation of the player who wishes to create such a character in the first place. Are they invested in exploring the lupine POV, with all the wonder, inhumanity, and spirituality that comes from such a deep connection to Gaia? Great. Looking to load up on gnosis out the gate to power a bunch of gifts? Not so great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker","name":"pwtucker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26645_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T10:58:34-07:00","id":1463600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pwtucker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463238-lupus-gnosis-issue?p=1463598#post1463598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think lupus falls into the same category as other challenging rp concepts, like Red Talons or reformed BSD or whatever. It can be done, but only by mature, thoughtful players who have enough experience to play such concepts responsibly. Thus I'd say the problem isn't with the numbers or concept, but the motivation of the player who wishes to create such a character in the first place. Are they invested in exploring the lupine POV, with all the wonder, inhumanity, and spirituality that comes from such a deep connection to Gaia? Great. Looking to load up on gnosis out the gate to power a bunch of gifts? Not so great.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm actually going to disagree with this. Because for casual play, all you need to do is watch movies like Watership Down and Plague Dogs. At the end of the day, those movies depict a decent way to portray a lupus-garou. After all, lupus have human reasoning.<br /> <br /> A lupus is a corebook splat, not an obscure camp. I've seen people roleplay very dark wolf RPs that would fit lupus characters just fine. The harder we treat playing lupus, the more they will be denied.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T12:21:03-07:00","id":1463605,"title":"","content":"It was probably a game design mistake to give different breeds different amount of Gnosis, and different tribes different amount of Willpower. Possibly even different Rage for the auspices (although at least the auspice angle has better justification in game). In early days of the game, you could tell who were the cheese players because they brought to the table their Lupus Stargazer Ahroun as this got them a lot of build points for free.<br /> <br /> A game like Vampire didn't have that problem because other than Clan weaknesses, you didn't have one group at a disadvantage or advantage over another. Traits like Willpower, max Blood Pool size, Humanity, etc. was all based on points spent elsewhere - certain Backgrounds or Virtues that any player could have chosen.<br /> <br /> If we wanted to go down a similar route, we could make all starting PCs have 1 each in Gnosis and Willpower (and possibly Rage) and then assign a certain number of Tempers points (I recall somewhere referring to this category as Tempers though I can't remember where, rename if needed) that a player can divide up however he sees fit. Maybe somewhere between 4-6 points or some other sensible number that is spent on a one to one basis. <br /> <br /> Maybe at this level we even state there is certain Maximum allowed per auspice or breed in certain categories at this stage, that can then be supplemented by Freebies. That's how the game handles Abilities restrictions for Lupus - certain skills are disallowed during the Ability 13/9/5 breakdown at character creation, but Freebies can spent on anything if you really want your Lupus to have points in Computer or Drive. Or we can dump any restrictions entirely. <br /> <br /> That way, no PC gets more build points than any other. That eliminates anyone from getting a build point advantage and would lead to players only picking tribes/auspice/breed based on their concept. We can always state that traditionally this auspice has more Rage than others, or that this breed has more Gnosis than others. And STs can even enforce this as part of NPC stats. But players can build their characters however they want, and no one is at a build point disadvantage than others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T13:27:30-07:00","id":1463609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463238-lupus-gnosis-issue?p=1463600#post1463600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm actually going to disagree with this. Because for casual play, all you need to do is watch movies like Watership Down and Plague Dogs. At the end of the day, those movies depict a decent way to portray a lupus-garou. After all, lupus have human reasoning.<br /> <br /> A lupus is a corebook splat, not an obscure camp. I've seen people roleplay very dark wolf RPs that would fit lupus characters just fine. The harder we treat playing lupus, the more they will be denied.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair enough. I've rarely seen a lupus played right, however. Tons of friendly doggo types, a few who act just like people with a penchant for only eating meat, and some who remember occasionally that they're supposed to have a wolf's background and bring it up.<br /> <br /> I'd also say that folks who'd take the time to watch Watership Down or read a book on wolves are already far, far ahead of the regular player. I'd agree that they'd probably do a great job. I'm talking about folks who think wolves are basically like angry dogs and don't take it any further.<br /> <br /> In my games, at least, lupus have a unique mindset, having only discovered causality, time, and other such abstract concepts upon their first change. Yes they are Garou, and have intelligence and the ability to reason and so forth, but it's all filtered through their original mindset, where hierarchy, nature, etc comes first, and the city and the Weaver and so forth are truly alien (in general.)<br /> <br /> Thus if someone wants to rock up with a lupus who could easily be a German Shepherd or just a guy who doesn't bathe often, and that's the extent of the flavor, it wouldn't work for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker","name":"pwtucker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26645_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T14:03:30-07:00","id":1463617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pwtucker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463238-lupus-gnosis-issue?p=1463609#post1463609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my games, at least, lupus have a unique mindset, having only discovered causality, time, and other such abstract concepts upon their first change. Yes they are Garou, and have intelligence and the ability to reason and so forth, but it's all filtered through their original mindset, where hierarchy, nature, etc comes first, and the city and the Weaver and so forth are truly alien (in general.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Wolves aren't that hierarchical, and definitely have some concept of time and causality. It is unlikely that they would have a moral concept of nature vs weaver. I don't know if they would find the city more alien than walking on two legs to begin with, either.<br /> <br /> Not to say that your take on them is wrong, but you have exactly the problem <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1008_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1008\" data-vbnamecard=\"1008\">heinrich</a> pointed out, a very narrow view of what is the true right way to play lupus. People are different, so are other mammals. What about a fictional race of wolf-people? Why different interpretations of how a Lupus should be like harm your game so much?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T14:27:24-07:00","id":1463621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463238-lupus-gnosis-issue?p=1463617#post1463617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wolves aren't that hierarchical, and definitely have some concept of time and causality. It is unlikely that they would have a moral concept of nature vs weaver. I don't know if they would find the city more alien than walking on two legs to begin with, either.<br /> <br /> Not to say that your take on them is wrong, but you have exactly the problem <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1008_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1008\" data-vbnamecard=\"1008\">heinrich</a> pointed out, a very narrow view of what is the true right way to play lupus. People are different, so are other mammals. What about a fictional race of wolf-people? Why different interpretations of how a Lupus should be like harm your game so much?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly. And it is never the crinos-born who get this treatment, even though they too live far from humanity and most grow up with working snouts and ears.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, as long as someone does not keep up the alpha myth and checks body language, if they play their lupus like a character from Balto, I won't care. Because at the end of the day? All of that is heavily background material, it might show up, but what is most important is that the lupus character won't be a burden on the group in the moment.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T15:00:23-07:00","id":1463626,"title":"","content":"Another thing that I find frustrating with the talk of how lupus &quot;should&quot; be portrayed: time.<br /> <br /> Lots of people seem to think the a lupus PC had their First Change, cub-hood, and Rite of Passage all within the last week of history, instead of years to adapt to their expanded mental state, the reality of the Garou world, and so on.<br /> <br /> I had a lupus I played for ~10 years in game (longer IRL time), who I created as having had his First Change four years before start. So that was 2 years as a wolf, 4 years as a Lost Cub/found Cub/training/etc. and 10 years of experience as a Garou out in the world. Some people would complain about him not being &quot;wolf&quot; enough, to which I had a simple response: he's been leaving around humans for three (then four, then five...) times longer than he was a ever just a wolf. If you spend four years living in another country with a very different culture, and a very different language, and you still couldn't act like a local even there's obvious tells you're not one... would people think you were even trying to learn how? Because if my lupus can pass as a human, he's doing something he's been practicing how to do for years. Thanks for the compliment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T15:29:45-07:00","id":1463630,"title":"","content":"One of my favorite canon Lupus character is IIRC a Wendigo/Lost Cub who still have no contact with other Garou, but taught themselves to live with humans enough to get a degree in History and a job at a library. The character went through the entire process from being little more than a wolf mind to acclimate to human society and find a place within it.<br /> <br /> And it is important to remember that Garou are different even before the First Change. Lupus already have strange minds that have an exceedingly hard time connecting to the rest of their wolf packs. They're maybe more human than wolf in mind, who knows?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T19:34:06-07:00","id":1463638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pwtucker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463238-lupus-gnosis-issue?p=1463609#post1463609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Fair enough. I've rarely seen a lupus played right, however. Tons of friendly doggo types, a few who act just like people with a penchant for only eating meat, and some who remember occasionally that they're supposed to have a wolf's background and bring it up.<br /> <br /> I'd also say that folks who'd take the time to watch Watership Down or read a book on wolves are already far, far ahead of the regular player. I'd agree that they'd probably do a great job. I'm talking about folks who think wolves are basically like angry dogs and don't take it any further.<br /> <br /> In my games, at least, lupus have a unique mindset, having only discovered causality, time, and other such abstract concepts upon their first change. Yes they are Garou, and have intelligence and the ability to reason and so forth, but it's all filtered through their original mindset, where hierarchy, nature, etc comes first, and the city and the Weaver and so forth are truly alien (in general.)<br /> <br /> Thus if someone wants to rock up with a lupus who could easily be a German Shepherd or just a guy who doesn't bathe often, and that's the extent of the flavor, it wouldn't work for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wolves probably already had a good deal of time and causality down already. There are some insights distilled down from sources in <i>Are We Smart Enough to Know How Smart Animals Are?</i> that can also help with wolves, to wit, as well as in <i>Mama's Last Hug</i>. for the emotional side of wildlife. One of the things that most distinguishes lupus is that they pay attention to humans and learn from them more readily, but not the way that domestic dogs do; it's more akin to the way humans pay attention to other humans, but it's still going to be off, in a &quot;wolf-spirit thing pretending to be human&quot; manner, like looking overly long at how vulnerable some behaviors make humans and filing them away for how to deal with them, perhaps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T03:31:37-07:00","id":1463681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463238-lupus-gnosis-issue?p=1463579#post1463579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I personally like 2/3/4 for the breeds.<br /> <br /> I don't think the non-homid breeds -need- extra XP, they have unique gifts and things they can call upon that homids cannot.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The idea is to make it like other games in which flaws do not give you build points, they grant you ways to give you extra experience when your character suffers because of the flaw, only applying it to inherent lupus and metis flaws. So, if a lupus in human form is persued by security because he took food and did not pay, he gets experience, and so on... It would reward good roleplay of the flaws, and incentivize players to put their characters in the 'bad' situations, instead of making them dread these situations.<br /> <br /> It could also apply to homids who would have difficulties dealing with wolves and werewolves, to make it even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T03:46:52-07:00","id":1463685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463238-lupus-gnosis-issue?p=1463626#post1463626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing that I find frustrating with the talk of how lupus &quot;should&quot; be portrayed: time.<br /> <br /> Lots of people seem to think the a lupus PC had their First Change, cub-hood, and Rite of Passage all within the last week of history, instead of years to adapt to their expanded mental state, the reality of the Garou world, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, fully agree. It often seems like the requirement for lupus PCs is to play a realistic wolf, rather than a half-human half-wolf creature that can reason. Thus, anything that might stray from that mentality is heavily penalized. Including the lupus cub being taught basics of Veil safety and blending in.<br /> <br /> Heck, in W20, even the Red Talons are stated to not just throw their cubs to the world with no Veil training. So non-Talons certainly would not just rush the RoP of a lupus.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T04:03:28-07:00","id":1463687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463238-lupus-gnosis-issue?p=1463681#post1463681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The idea is to make it like other games in which flaws do not give you build points, they grant you ways to give you extra experience when your character suffers because of the flaw, only applying it to inherent lupus and metis flaws. So, if a lupus in human form is persued by security because he took food and did not pay, he gets experience, and so on... It would reward good roleplay of the flaws, and incentivize players to put their characters in the 'bad' situations, instead of making them dread these situations.<br /> <br /> It could also apply to homids who would have difficulties dealing with wolves and werewolves, to make it even.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I vastly prefer this approach to flaws/weakness/etc. as a a design aesthetic, just tossing it into a WtA game as-is would make the mechanic feel really out of place.<br /> <br /> You also have to be careful with how the rewards are phrased. The Garou-born are easier to apply this to because there's a huge amount of social and mechanical stuff enforced by the game against them.<br /> <br /> Lupus don't really have much in this regard. Not paying for something is a Cub mistake, not a Lupus mistake. Wolves might not think about property like humans do, but they understand that there are consequences for taking something someone else has laid a claim to. And that's normal wolves, not Lupus with their much more human-like mind. The Lupus ability restrictions also only apply to character creation. In play they can snag dots in anything they don't have at start. There's no surcharge, no special learning requirements, etc. <br /> <br /> If you're not careful you make Lupus unnecessarily unpopular because you end up rewarding them for Fishmalk style behavior because their players get XP for being bad at pretending to be being human instead of good at being a wolf.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T08:56:14-07:00","id":1463705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463238-lupus-gnosis-issue?p=1463681#post1463681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The idea is to make it like other games in which flaws do not give you build points, they grant you ways to give you extra experience when your character suffers because of the flaw, only applying it to inherent lupus and metis flaws. So, if a lupus in human form is persued by security because he took food and did not pay, he gets experience, and so on... It would reward good roleplay of the flaws, and incentivize players to put their characters in the 'bad' situations, instead of making them dread these situations.<br /> <br /> It could also apply to homids who would have difficulties dealing with wolves and werewolves, to make it even.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that it's not going to be equal even if applied the other way, because there are so few lupus and wolves and so many more humans and homid Garou. Imperfectly getting along with rats would be a huge handicap in Ratkin society (which is heavily angled away from humanity because there are way more rodens Ratkin than homid), but for Garou, not quite getting wolf behavior is only going to mean that you don't send them to the Red Talon caern on business. Not alone, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T09:24:32-07:00","id":1463707,"title":"","content":"I have to say that I find it weird and confusing the ideas people have about &quot;being inhuman&quot; or &quot;interpreting a wolf/animal/undead/whatever&quot;.<br /> <br /> As an autistic person and in contact with many other neurodivergent people, I'm pretty used to have an &quot;inhuman&quot; mindset as many would describe it (sometimes to my face). A &quot;human&quot; one puzzles me far more. And yet I see a lot of nonsensical assumptions that actually have nothing to do with not thinking like a normal person, instead have to do with behaving like a completely normal person expects your stereotype should behave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T09:32:01-07:00","id":1463709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463238-lupus-gnosis-issue?p=1463707#post1463707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say that I find it weird and confusing the ideas people have about &quot;being inhuman&quot; or &quot;interpreting a wolf/animal/undead/whatever&quot;.<br /> <br /> As an autistic person and in contact with many other neurodivergent people, I'm pretty used to have an &quot;inhuman&quot; mindset as many would describe it (sometimes to my face). A &quot;human&quot; one puzzles me far more. And yet I see a lot of nonsensical assumptions that actually have nothing to do with not thinking like a normal person, instead have to do with behaving like a completely normal person expects your stereotype should behave.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here, actually. I have MUCH easier time playing a crinos-born or a lupus than a homid, because a lot of my social derps are not as visible then. When I play a homid, I have immensely more difficulty portraying one believably to other players.<br /> <br /> Not helped by the fact most games are set in the USA and I'm not American XD<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T09:54:41-07:00","id":1463714,"title":"","content":"Lots of great points and discussion. My POV seems to be in the minority, and that's fine - I only play a table top game, so it's not as if I'm imposing my view on anybody outside of four other like-minded players.<br /> <br /> That said, I think what informs my POV is that homids tend to act very 'human' and thus I ask that lupus players at my table act very 'lupine', just as I ask that metis adopt a different POV and way of seeing the world as well. Obviously what that means will vary enormously, but my understanding is to be more literal, more in tune with nature, more hierarchical (because the game itself has alpha's and the like embedded into Garou culture), and so forth. <br /> <br /> Definitely not arguing that anybody else is wrong, just that I personally set a high bar for what I consider an accurate lupus representation, and that anyone wanting to play one do some research and think it through before making a grab for the 5 gnosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker","name":"pwtucker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26645_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T10:01:41-07:00","id":1463715,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=pwtucker;n1463714<br /> That said, I think what informs my POV is that homids tend to act very 'human' and thus I ask that lupus players at my table act very 'lupine', just as I ask that metis adopt a different POV and way of seeing the world as well. Obviously what that means will vary enormously, but my understanding is to be more literal, more in tune with nature, more hierarchical (because the game itself has alpha's and the like embedded into Garou culture), and so forth.<br /> [/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Garou are hierarical, but not lupus. WtA books have actually multiple times disowned the alpha myth entirely. Best has to be Shadow Lord revised which dedicated a whole PAGE explaining how dumb it is to wolves.<br /> <br /> Not directed at you, pwtucker, but I feel a lot of people see wolves as living in the deep woods and never having much interaction with things outside the woods. But wolves are found all around and unlike, say, Red Talons who conciously try to avoid too many human things, a wolf would not say no to roadkill or a trashcan. Wolves aren't inherently more dignified than humans, in fact I'd say HUMANS have much more dignity than animals who roll in corpses and eat fisheads only.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T10:15:21-07:00","id":1463718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pwtucker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463238-lupus-gnosis-issue?p=1463714#post1463714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely not arguing that anybody else is wrong, just that I personally set a high bar for what I consider an accurate lupus representation, and that anyone wanting to play one do some research and think it through before making a grab for the 5 gnosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is fair to want a high bar <b>because</b> the game gives 5 Gnosis to the char. The problem is that isn't solving anything, really. Your high bar isn't more realistic and it isn't changing the actual problem, that is a PC grabbing 5 Gnosis just 'cause. The only thing it is doing is reward players with a strict view of a Lupus with 5 Gnosis while denying players with different views the same benefit. What's more, putting on the player the responsibility of prepping like a professional actor for a game.<br /> <br /> But this isn't your problem, it is a problem from the game, and an old one. The Gnosis distribution is stupid, and the biggest flaw of White Wolf was always its pedantry, encouraging the players to do exactly that, correct the failures in the rules through their actor skills instead of by asking for better rules.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if your high bar is working for you that's good enough. I wouldn't make it even to interpret a human being, maybe a Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T10:29:16-07:00","id":1463720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463238-lupus-gnosis-issue?p=1463715#post1463715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Garou are hierarical, but not lupus. WtA books have actually multiple times disowned the alpha myth entirely. Best has to be Shadow Lord revised which dedicated a whole PAGE explaining how dumb it is to wolves.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty fascinating. I've not seen that in any of the books, but then again, I've not read most of the tribe books. Thanks for pointing that out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker","name":"pwtucker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26645_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T10:32:26-07:00","id":1463721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463238-lupus-gnosis-issue?p=1463718#post1463718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is fair to want a high bar <b>because</b> the game gives 5 Gnosis to the char. The problem is that isn't solving anything, really. Your high bar isn't more realistic and it isn't changing the actual problem, that is a PC grabbing 5 Gnosis just 'cause. The only thing it is doing is reward players with a strict view of a Lupus with 5 Gnosis while denying players with different views the same benefit. What's more, putting on the player the responsibility of prepping like a professional actor for a game.<br /> <br /> But this isn't your problem, it is a problem from the game, and an old one. The Gnosis distribution is stupid, and the biggest flaw of White Wolf was always its pedantry, encouraging the players to do exactly that, correct the failures in the rules through their actor skills instead of by asking for better rules.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if your high bar is working for you that's good enough. I wouldn't make it even to interpret a human being, maybe a Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd phrase it a little differently: I set the high bar for rp purposes, and if I find the player can meet that I'm fine with them taking the 5 gnosis or any other powerful benefit (fetish, merit, etc) because I'll trust them to play that element correctly. Then again, in our games we don't really use xp much, or renown, as instead we just grow our characters' sheets as the PC's themselves grow, and the stats tend to reflect the RP. Clearly a case of everyone's mileage varying pretty intensely. <br /> <br /> Anyways, I appreciate your discussing this with me, and causing me to stop and think about what I'd always just accepted as part of the game. Much appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker","name":"pwtucker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26645_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T05:31:05-07:00","id":1464012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463238-lupus-gnosis-issue?p=1463687#post1463687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I vastly prefer this approach to flaws/weakness/etc. as a a design aesthetic, just tossing it into a WtA game as-is would make the mechanic feel really out of place.<br /> <br /> You also have to be careful with how the rewards are phrased. The Garou-born are easier to apply this to because there's a huge amount of social and mechanical stuff enforced by the game against them.<br /> <br /> Lupus don't really have much in this regard. Not paying for something is a Cub mistake, not a Lupus mistake. Wolves might not think about property like humans do, but they understand that there are consequences for taking something someone else has laid a claim to. And that's normal wolves, not Lupus with their much more human-like mind. The Lupus ability restrictions also only apply to character creation. In play they can snag dots in anything they don't have at start. There's no surcharge, no special learning requirements, etc.<br /> <br /> If you're not careful you make Lupus unnecessarily unpopular because you end up rewarding them for Fishmalk style behavior because their players get XP for being bad at pretending to be being human instead of good at being a wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sure, the possibility of players overdoing is an issue. In the games I've seen it used, it's generally limited to once per session, so it shouldn't be an issue. But eh, as we can see in this thread, what's a fishmalk roleplay for one storyteller may not be not nearly damn enough for the next one. <br /> <br /> But I still think it's better to have players wanting to act their flaws than having the players cash up first and then conveniently forget the flaws. Being flaw police is not that fun for the storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T08:32:33-07:00","id":1464036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463238-lupus-gnosis-issue?p=1464012#post1464012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I still think it's better to have players wanting to act their flaws than having the players cash up first and then conveniently forget the flaws. Being flaw police is not that fun for the storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>But doing this XP thing is being Flaw police all the same.<br /> <br /> The core problem is still that giving differing amounts of starting points to a character based on a choice is a shitty design. And instead of solving the shitty design, the game uses &quot;RP flaws&quot; to put the onus of correcting balance in the players and encourage the ST to punish/reward them for RP as if it were actor school.<br /> <br /> I personally loved what they did with the Seemings in C20. They had the same problem, the difference between Childling, Wilder and Grump was point distribution between Banality and Glamour. Less severe than the insanity of Breed, but still the same core issue. In C20 they ditched it almost completely and instead made each Seeming be immune to a particular source of Banality. This is wonderful, as it encourages expected behavior in a very broad term without punishing anyone.<br /> <br /> Breed should do the same. Make for each an additional way to restore WP, Rage and Gnosis, for example, related to their themes. Or a single aditional way to earn any of those and define that Homids get WP, Metis get Rage and Lupus get Gnosis. Then everyone starts with Gnosis 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T12:40:40-07:00","id":1464067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463238-lupus-gnosis-issue?p=1464036#post1464036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But doing this XP thing is being Flaw police all the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really.<br /> <br /> When it's pay-forward, it's in their best interests to <b>not remind</b> the ST of their character's flaws. Having to constantly say that someone's roleplay is not appropriate tends to make things more <b>adversarial</b>. <br /> <br /> When it's active-reward, the players roleplay their flaws, and then they <b>gently remind</b> the ST of their character's flaws they are roleplaying, because it's in their best interests to do so. Rewarding for roleplay their flaws makes them <b>happy </b>to do it.<br /> <br /> At least, that's what's happened in my experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T15:33:02-07:00","id":1464095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463238-lupus-gnosis-issue?p=1464012#post1464012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, the possibility of players overdoing is an issue. In the games I've seen it used, it's generally limited to once per session, so it shouldn't be an issue. But eh, as we can see in this thread, what's a fishmalk roleplay for one storyteller may not be not nearly damn enough for the next one.<br /> <br /> But I still think it's better to have players wanting to act their flaws than having the players cash up first and then conveniently forget the flaws. Being flaw police is not that fun for the storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need to sell me on the idea of the design tool of using XP as a reward for Flaws as they impact the character rather than giving players extra build points for taking flaws. I much prefer the reward later approach.<br /> <br /> My points are more specifically:<br /> <br /> 1) Plopping a reward later mechanic into an otherwise points up front game doesn't work. If you want to completely redo WtA's XP systems, that's cool, but it's a bit beyond the scope here.<br /> <br /> 2) The downside of the reward later approach is that you need to make sure the rewards incentivize the behavior you want. This isn't about the ST Flaw police as it is on the game designers. How the game designers describe what the XP rewards triggers are is what the ST and players are going to react to. As I said, you need to make sure any such approach reinforces playing up a characters non-human upbringing rather than reinforcing playing up being disruptive with &quot;well I wasn't born human,&quot; as a rationale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T17:56:50-07:00","id":1464116,"title":"","content":"Following my own idea, I'm brainstorming a rule to my liking. The idea for now is for every character to start with Gnosis 3 and Breed gives a special benefit when following specific tenets of the Litany:<br /> <br /> <b> - Homid - <u>Submission to Those of Higher Station</u></b><br /> True wolves aren't creature of hierarchy. Humans are. Be it a boss or a god, following the vision of another is a human instinct to validate your own actions.<br /> <i>When a Homid takes a decision based on being ordered to do so, gain a Willpower Point</i>.<br /> <br /> <b> - Metis - <u>Combat the Wyrm Wherever it Dwells and Whenever it Breeds</u></b><br /> Born in Garou society, the war for Gaia is their cultural birthright. It gives then purpose, it channels their anger, and they have no previous beliefs or impulses for it to conflict with.<br /> <i>When a Metis starts combat with a minion of the Wyrm, gain a Rage Point</i>.<br /> <br /> <b> - Lupus - <u>Accept an Honorable Surrender</u></b><br /> Lacking complex language, wolves communicate through action. Fighting among themselves isn't about enmity, winning or causing harm, but making statements.<br /> <i>When a Lupus accepts a surrender without further aggression, gain a Gnosis Point</i>.<br /> <br /> Here's my first draft, please comment, I need suggestions to polish it. The idea is to encourage those behaviors in the loosest terms possible, to make room for interpretation. Homids get WP from devotion and/or discipline, Metis get Rage from following the goal of the Garou in its purest and most direct form, Lupus get Gnosis from talking with their bodies more than their mouths. All of them are being rewarded when they default to their &quot;Breed Strategy&quot; to make decisions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T18:36:34-07:00","id":1464121,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I like linking it to the Litany like this. I get how you got there from C20, but the Litany isn't really the same as Banality.<br /> <br /> I'd consider Renown instead. Something like, &quot;whenever a PC gains [Rank + 1] temporary Renown for their linked Renown category, in a single scene, they also get a temporary point of Willpower/Rage/Gnosis.&quot;<br /> <br /> Homids would go with Honor, as Honor represents the complex learned social contracts that Homids are more used to navigating from their humanity.<br /> <br /> Garou-born would go with Glory, as noted they're indoctrinated the most to the warrior culture of the Garou, and easily develop a strong desire to prove themselves in the light of the negative views the Nation has of them.<br /> <br /> Lupus would go with Wisdom, as Garou Wisdom leans more into natural and instinctual intelligence over book learning, which the mix of wolf and human mind of the lupus tend to have a strong affinity for.<br /> <br /> Even then, regain Willpower, Rage, and Gnosis are also radically difficult in how hard they are to regain. Rage even risks being more of a drawback than a bonus if it drives your Rage too high.<br /> <br /> It might be worth sticking closer to C20 and going to the only real WtA mechanic with multiple triggers: Frenzy. Each Breed having an easier time resisting (or outright ignoring) certain Frenzy triggers might work out better as something that's easier to balance in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T19:51:06-07:00","id":1464135,"title":"","content":"Going back to the drawing board because this was really useful. Te Litany was the first thing that came to mind, but both Renown and Frenzy are indeed better options. I'll stick to Frenzy for the next iteration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T20:11:35-07:00","id":1464136,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> <br /> <br /> If you like the Frenzy idea, a suggestion for how to go about it:<br /> <br /> Homids: Growing up with a relatively frail human body, they get a +2 difficulty to Frenzy checks from feelings of confinement or helplessness, however the high value human societies put on social standing leaves them more sensitive to the perceptions of others and hits them with a -2 penalty to Frenzy checks from embarrassment and humiliation.<br /> <br /> Garou-born: Coping with the regular heaping on of negativity from others, they internalize the message or harden their hearts to it, gaining a +2 difficulty bonus against taunt inspired Frenzy checks, however knowing that none of their forms are safe from silver, they can't help but react stronger than others towards it and receive a -2 difficulty modifier when large quantities of silver are around.<br /> <br /> Lupus:Failure is a natural part of a wolf's life, sometimes prey gets away, sometimes a challenge to realign a pack's social pecking order doesn't work out, but survival requires to not dwell and move on. As such the lupus get a +2 Difficulty bonus to resist Frenzies from embarrassment or humiliation unless... they end up endangering their pack severely, as they suffer a -2 difficulty penalty when the see their packmates get injured.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T20:38:32-07:00","id":1464145,"title":"","content":"Second try:<br /> <br /> Each Breed has two effects, immunity to one trigger and a benefit on one aspect of Rage. I'm not sure if only one of those is enough and either way it will present two options for each for us to discuss.<br /> <br /> <b>- Homid - </b><br /> Large quantities of silver in the area - Humans love the stuff and are used to deal with things they shouldn't, like poisons and allergies. A nervous human is more alert or even excited than flighty.<br /> Beast Within: Humans are also excellent at hiding their will to kill. A Homid doesn't suffer from the Beast Within even with high Rage.<br /> <br /> <b>- Metis - </b><br /> Any strong emotion - They're taunted and mistreated since they're born. At the time of their First Change they're seething with all kinds of emotions. Without this most Metis wouldn't ever be out of frenzy.<br /> Losing the Wolf: Reverting to their breed won't do much to get them out of touch with Rage. A Metis never loses the Wolf.<br /> <br /> <b>- Lupus - </b><br /> Embarrassment or humiliation - Wolves can sense this, but to a far lesser degree than humans, as true humiliation is a complex social construct that is second nature to humans, but a learned abstraction to the Lupus.<br /> Remaining Active: Be it to run for shelter or protect pack and cubs, acting out of desperation isn't strange for wolves. Lupus never Frenzy from rolls to Remain Active.<br /> <br /> Incidentally I got to remember how much I don't like the rules for Thrall of the Wyrm. It is gratuitous drama and disgusting behavior, but since it is on corpses it have no actual stakes for most situations. It is just a WTF moment with a recommendation to kill your character if you have a bad roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":"10-16-2021, 05:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T00:04:03-07:00","id":1464162,"title":"","content":"I'm not so sure about the Homid options. Homids, in the human skins, don't take special damage from silver. So the reasoning there feels off (and Lupus get the same benefit in their Breed form). I'm also not really that confident that Homids are particularly good at hiding their urge to kill. Beast Within applies to all social rolls, not just dealing with humans. A Homid in Crinos/Hispo/Lupus is less experienced with hiding their emotions in forms that rely on completely different forms of communication, and that means being able to hide their Rage from other supernaturally sensitive creatures.<br /> <br /> For the Lupus, never Frenzying on Remain Active is a much bigger bonus than the others considering the difference it makes in combat.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T02:38:12-07:00","id":1464166,"title":"","content":"I didn't understand about the Homid with silver. The rule would be that being around lots of silver don't trigger Frenzy, something that by RAW occur even in Breed form despite not taking Agg. And the reasoning is that we do things like cooking poison to eat and decorate our living room with deadly plants, so surrounding yourself with stuff you shouldn't be handling is par of the course.<br /> <br /> The hiding intent to kill have to do, again, more with intent than skill. A lupus may be better at hiding emotions in wolf form, but it won't want to frequently, wolves don't deal a lot in hiding their emotions to draw in their victims (internal or external). A homid may face a lot of difficulty, but learning to hide emotions and intent is one of the first things they'll even think to do, as they're still wired to think of it as a faux pas at the very least.<br /> <br /> What do you think of Remain Active having +2 successes in the Frenzy thresholds for Lupus instead of plain immunity?<br /> <br /> Otherwise do you have suggestions for me to try instead of those? What do you think of it overall?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T05:01:44-07:00","id":1464172,"title":"","content":"My point about Homids and silver is just that since silver isn't that dangerous to them in homid, then it doesn't really qualify for the idea that humans like to surround themselves with dangerous things. Most of the time Homids are going to be around silver in quantity, they're unlikely to be in a form where it's dangerous to them. You don't go to a fancy party with true silver flatware and serving dishes in Crinos.<br /> <br /> On emotions... there's a big difference between hiding your emotions, and not being affected by them. Humans are very emotional creatures and it's not really that hard to get us to get very angry or very scared if emotions get too intense.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure there's a way to make Remain Active feel right comparatively. The Beast Within and Losing the Wolf are both things you can just avoid. You can make sure your WP is significantly higher than your Rage so The Beast Within never gets out even with a few temp. Rage over normal. You can avoid Losing the Wolf by just not spending that last point. Remaining active can come up any time you take a lot of damage, and there's no way to avoid the Frenzy for anyone else. <br /> <br /> As for suggestions... how did you feel about the ideas I posted above?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T05:26:56-07:00","id":1464176,"title":"","content":"Confinement and Helplessness may work. At first I thought against it because I imagine being trust again into such situations wouldn't be nice, but in the end is the same reasoning of Metis, so yeah. For the Metis I prefer the strong emotions because going by the book it is simpler to define, and they deserve/need this as socially being a Metis sucks <b><u>a lot</u></b>. I also had this thought that they get used to being taunted by less physically capable people, which would be covered by RAW by the Strong Emotions part, but being effectively taunted by stronger Garou isn't something they specially deal with, as those would avoid then instead before First Change.<br /> <br /> I prefer to keep then as flat out immunity, as I feel it is simpler and works better towards the goal of encouraging behavior. And I really enjoyed the idea of adding non-Frenzy aspects of Rage, but Remain Active is really out of question now that I look at it with more attention. I don't <b>want</b> to scrap the whole idea and keep just the Frenzy triggers, but I <b>can</b> do so if this ends up being better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T05:36:20-07:00","id":1464177,"title":"","content":"Actually, an alternative for Lupus instead of Remaining Active?<br /> <br /> They don't Frenzy from staredowns (which uses the higher of your Rage or Intimidation dice pool, and if you end up using Rage you can Frenzy from it). Wolves are much more acclimated to that sort of simple dominance display/contest and thus aren't going to fly off the handle if they try to use their Rage in such a fashion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T06:06:47-07:00","id":1464182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463238-lupus-gnosis-issue?p=1464177#post1464177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't Frenzy from staredowns (which uses the higher of your Rage or Intimidation dice pool, and if you end up using Rage you can Frenzy from it). Wolves are much more acclimated to that sort of simple dominance display/contest and thus aren't going to fly off the handle if they try to use their Rage in such a fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect! I completely forgot this one!<br /> <br /> Well, with those tweaks, lets go to the third iteration:<br /> <br /> Each Breed has two effects, immunity to one trigger and a benefit on one aspect of Rage. Starting Gnosis is always 3.<br /> <br /> <b>- Homid -</b><br /> <i>Confinement</i> and <i>Helplessness</i> - Humans are frail, but also used to live with such sensations to navigate their environment. Boxes are confined and waiting for help is jarring, but elevator beats stairs and 911 beats fighting for your life.<br /> <b>Beast Within:</b> Humans learn quickly to at least try to hide their will to kill. A <b>Homid</b> doesn't suffer from the <i>Beast Within</i> even with high <b>Rage</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>- Metis -</b><br /> <i>Any strong emotion</i> - They're taunted and mistreated since they're born. At the time of their First Change they're seething with all kinds of emotions. Without this most <b>Metis</b> wouldn't ever be out of frenzy.<br /> <b>Losing the Wolf:</b> Reverting to their breed won't do much to get them out of touch with <b>Rage</b>. A <b>Metis</b> never <i>Loses the Wolf</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>- Lupus -</b><br /> <i>Embarrassment or humiliation</i> - Wolves can feel then, but to a far lesser degree than humans as true humiliation is a complex social construct that is second nature to humans, but a learned abstraction to the <b>Lupus</b>.<br /> <b>Stare Down:</b> Without verbal language, challenges among wolves are tools for communication, not aggression. <b>Lupus</b> never Frenzy when using <b>Rage</b> on <i>Stare Down</i> contests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T06:43:36-07:00","id":1464190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463238-lupus-gnosis-issue?p=1464182#post1464182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perfect! I completely forgot this one!<br /> <br /> Well, with those tweaks, lets go to the third iteration:<br /> <br /> Each Breed has two effects, immunity to one trigger and a benefit on one aspect of Rage. Starting Gnosis is always 3.<br /> <br /> <b>- Homid -</b><br /> <i>Confinement</i> and <i>Helplessness</i> - Humans are frail, but also used to live with such sensations to navigate their environment. Boxes are confined and waiting for help is jarring, but elevator beats stairs and 911 beats fighting for your life.<br /> <b>Beast Within:</b> Humans learn quickly to at least try to hide their will to kill. A <b>Homid</b> doesn't suffer from the <i>Beast Within</i> even with high <b>Rage</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>- Metis -</b><br /> <i>Any strong emotion</i> - They're taunted and mistreated since they're born. At the time of their First Change they're seething with all kinds of emotions. Without this most <b>Metis</b> wouldn't ever be out of frenzy.<br /> <b>Losing the Wolf:</b> Reverting to their breed won't do much to get them out of touch with <b>Rage</b>. A <b>Metis</b> never <i>Loses the Wolf</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>- Lupus -</b><br /> <i>Embarrassment or humiliation</i> - Wolves can feel then, but to a far lesser degree than humans as true humiliation is a complex social construct that is second nature to humans, but a learned abstraction to the <b>Lupus</b>.<br /> <b>Stare Down:</b> Without verbal language, challenges among wolves are tools for communication, not aggression. <b>Lupus</b> never Frenzy when using <b>Rage</b> on <i>Stare Down</i> contests.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are cool. The homid one actually being useful in wider things than just play, because people so want their homids to have day to day jobs. So there's a solution.<br /> <br /> The lupus one is clever, because a lot of people forget that wolves use body language to communicate.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T15:39:03-07:00","id":1464225,"title":"","content":"Seems very solid for this approach to things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}